# Portfolio redesign knowledgebase

This branch (`portfolio-redesign`) starts from a **blank** home / about / contact surface. Do not delete the prior redesign — reuse it as reference when building the new design.

## Prior UI (reference only)

- Components + board CSS: `app/redesign/`
- Conventions for animated project cards: `.cursor/rules/redesign-project-cards.mdc` (Grove as reference)
- Project metadata used by those cards: `app/redesign/projects.ts`
- Contact links: `app/redesign/contact-links.ts`

## Prior assets (reuse when they fit)

Root: `public/images/redesign/`

| Folder | Contents |
|--------|----------|
| `assets/` | Animated avatar SVG parts |
| `fredy/` | Portrait, California flag, download icon |
| `grove/` | Phone, plants, widgets, progress card |
| `tidehaus/` | Desktop, surfboard, snorkel |
| `sea-sky/` | Phone + feature icons |
| `selah/` | Phone frames, cross |
| `ziplearn/` | Phone + feature icons |
| `samples/` | Storefront + tool icons |
| `stack/` | Tool tiles (Figma, React, etc.) |
| `about/` | Photos, flags, activities, Duolingo, map |
| `contact/` | Portrait, button/media backgrounds |
| `breathe/` | Rive sprout breathing animation |

Case-study pages and project assets under `app/projects/` and `public/projects/` stay as-is; they are not part of the blank slate.

## Working rule

Build the new portfolio into `app/(portfolio)/` (and new components as needed). Treat `app/redesign/` + `public/images/redesign/` as a library of proven patterns and assets, not as the live site.

## Animation (new redesign)

**Use GSAP only** (`gsap`, plus plugins like `ScrollTrigger` when needed) for all new portfolio-redesign motion.

- Do **not** add new `motion` / `framer-motion` usage in the redesign surface.
- Prior redesign code in `app/redesign/` still uses `motion/react` — leave that alone as reference; do not port it unless asked.
- Existing in-repo GSAP examples: `app/webgl-test/demos/ScrollCamera.tsx`, `app/projects/selah-reflect/DotGrid.tsx`.
- Prefer cleanup in `useEffect` / `useLayoutEffect` (kill tweens, revert contexts, kill ScrollTriggers) and honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.
